00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:16.892
This is Anthropic, Read Aloud. Today: Anthropic announces closing of initial public offering, including full exercise of underwriters’ option to purchase additional shares, and closing of concurrent private placement.

2
00:00:18.192 --> 00:00:29.069
Anthropic announces closing of initial public offering, including full exercise of underwriters’ option to purchase additional shares, and closing of concurrent private placement.

3
00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:34.030
From Anthropic Newsroom, published November 20, 2026.

4
00:00:35.030 --> 00:01:02.976
Today Anthropic, P B C announced the closing of its initial public offering of an aggregate of 1127000000 shares of its Class A common stock at a public offering price of 83.00 dollarsper share, including the full exercise by the underwriters of their option to purchase an additional 147000000 shares of Class A common stock from Anthropic at the initial public offering price.

5
00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:36.456
The offering consisted of 1103351354 shares sold by Anthropic and 23648646 shares sold by certain selling stockholders. The aggregate gross proceeds from the offering, before deducting underwriting discounts and commissions and other offering expenses, were approximately 93.5 dollarsbillion, of which approximately 91.6 dollarsbillion was received by Anthropic.

6
00:01:36.576 --> 00:01:41.768
Anthropic did not receive any proceeds from the sale of shares by the selling stockholders.

7
00:01:42.218 --> 00:01:51.560
Anthropic’s Class A common stock began trading on the Nasdaq Global Select Market on November 19, 2026 under the symbol “ANT.”

8
00:01:52.010 --> 00:02:16.436
In addition to the shares of Class A common stock sold in the initial public offering, Anthropic closed the concurrent sale of an aggregate of 313253007 shares of Class N common stock to Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., Broadcom Inc., Google LLC, Micron Technology, Inc., Microsoft Corporation, NVIDIA Corporation, and TSMC Partners,

9
00:02:16.556 --> 00:02:28.819
Ltd. at the public offering price of 83.00 dollarsper share, in a private placement for an aggregate purchase price of approximately 26.0 dollarsbillion.

10
00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:38.527
The sale of these shares of Class N common stock was not registered under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended (the “Securities Act”).

11
00:02:38.647 --> 00:02:56.582
Aggregate gross proceeds from the initial public offering, including the shares sold by the selling stockholders, and the concurrent private placement were approximately 119.5 dollarsbillion, before deducting underwriting discounts and commissions and other offering expenses.

12
00:02:57.032 --> 00:03:17.298
Goldman Sachs and Co. LLC and Morgan Stanley acted as lead book-running managers for the offering. J.P. Morgan, Citigroup, Barclays, Wells Fargo Securities, BofA Securities, Deutsche Bank Securities, RBC Capital Markets, and UBS Investment Bank acted as book-running managers for the offering.

13
00:03:17.418 --> 00:03:36.608
BMO Capital Markets, BNP Paribas, Credit Agricole CIB, Jefferies, Mizuho, MUFG, and TD Securities acted as additional book-running managers for the offering. BTIG, Cantor, Capital One Securities, Macquarie Capital, and Societe Generale acted as co-managers for the offering.

14
00:03:37.058 --> 00:04:01.545
A registration statement relating to these securities was declared effective by the Securities and Exchange Commission on November 18, 2026, and a related registration statement filed pursuant to Rule 462(b) under the Securities Act became effective upon filing on November 18, 2026. The offering was made only by means of a prospectus.

15
00:04:01.665 --> 00:04:25.529
Copies of the final prospectus may be obtained from: Goldman Sachs and Co. LLC, Attention: Prospectus Department, 200 West Street, New York, NY 10282, by telephone at (866) 471 to 2526, or by email at prospectus-ny@ny.email.gs.com; or Morgan Stanley and Co.

16
00:04:25.649 --> 00:04:37.880
LLC, Attention: Prospectus Department, 180 Varick Street, 2nd Floor, New York, NY 10014, or by email at prospectus@morganstanley.com.

17
